{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "cism_thermo_discretization",
  "description": "Local EarthSciDiscretizations-format discretization rule for the CISM vertical temperature operator (stage 2 of the EqESM project; CISM = cismwrap_3_00_002 as built in CESM cesm3.0-alphabranch, glissade_therm.F90:1324-1507 glissade_temperature_matrix_elements, whichtemp = TEMP_PROGNOSTIC): the node-centered finite-volume diffusion of rhoi*shci*dT/dt = d/dz(coni*dT/dz) + rhoi*shci*Phi on the CISM sigma grid, where the temperature nodes sit at sigma_node = [sigma(1), stagsigma(1..upn-1), sigma(upn)] (surface sigma(1) = 0, bed sigma(upn) = 1; stagsigma are the layer midpoints) and the control volume of node n spans the CISM layer [sigma(n-1), sigma(n)] of width thck*dsigma_cv[n]. This file declares its own 1-D column grid contract (metaparameter UPN, index set lev_nodes of size UPN+1) rather than importing grids/column_nonuniform_1d of EarthSciDiscretizations, because the ESD column rules are lev-centered (state at cell centers, rules/varcoeff_face_laplacian_lev_flux_bc) while CISM's temperature is node-based (lev_nodes-shaped) with the control-volume faces at the sigma LEVELS, which are not the midpoints of the temperature nodes - the CISM operator is exactly the flux difference (G[n+1]-G[n])/(thck*dsigma_cv[n]) with the interface flux G[n] = K*(u[n]-u[n-1])/(thck*(sigma_node[n]-sigma_node[n-1])) (the Fortran dups stencil, glissade_therm.F90:151-163: dups(k,1)*dT = dT/((sigma(k+1)-sigma(k))*(stagsigma(k)-stagsigma(k-1))) with stagsigma(0)=sigma(1), dups(k,2)*dT = dT/((sigma(k+1)-sigma(k))*(stagsigma(k+1)-stagsigma(k))) with stagsigma(upn)=sigma(upn)). Boundary rows: row 1 (the surface node) lowers to 0 - the surface temperature is a Dirichlet value pinned separately (temp(0) = min(0, artm), F90:843, matrix row 1: diag = 1, rhsd = temp(0), F90:1405-1408) so its rate over a step is 0 except at the re-pin jumps - and row UPN+1 (the bed node) lowers to 0 - the bed temperature is NOT a diffusion row in CISM: the basal matrix row is the algebraic flux balance of the basal BC (F90:1473-1476), carried in the consuming model. The rule is the documented starting point for a future node-centered column-rule PR to EarthSciDiscretizations (the generalization: boundary rows closed against consumer-supplied flux or Dirichlet free names, and an interface-array coefficient K[n] instead of the CISM constant coni). Free names in the rule body (thck, sigma_node, dsigma_cv) resolve against the consuming model's declared parameters (esm-spec 9.6.1), following the consumer-supplied-geometry contract of the ESD rules; thck is the ice thickness (m) and sigma_node / dsigma_cv are the dimensionless node coordinates and layer widths of the CISM sigma grid.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "esd:rule",
   "family:finite_volume",
   "grid:cism_sigma_column",
   "op:varcoeff_laplacian",
   "axes:lev_nodes",
   "order:2",
   "stencil_width:3",
   "bc:dirichlet_surface",
   "spec:9.6.8"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "CISM (Community Ice Sheet Model) cism_main_3.00.002, libglissade/glissade_therm.F90 glissade_temperature_matrix_elements (F90:1324-1507) and the dups grid quantities (F90:151-163)."
   },
   {
    "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2007). Finite Difference Methods for Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations. SIAM. Section 2.13 (nonuniform grids)."
   }
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "UPN": { "type": "integer", "default": 11, "description": "Number of CISM sigma levels (layer interfaces); the temperature nodes number UPN+1 (k = 0 surface .. k = UPN bed, temperature at the layer midpoints plus the two boundary faces)." }
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "lev_nodes": { "kind": "interval", "size": { "op": "+", "args": ["UPN", 1] } }
 },
 "expression_templates": {
  "cism_interface_flux": {
   "description": "Diffusive flux K du/dz through ONE interior CISM sigma face n (2 <= n <= UPN): the face at sigma(n) lies between the temperature nodes n-1 and n (nodes 1 and UPN+1 are the surface and bed faces), and CISM evaluates the gradient between the two adjacent NODES: G[n] = K*(u[n]-u[n-1])/(thck*(sigma_node[n]-sigma_node[n-1])), the exact dups stencil of glissade_temperature_matrix_elements (glissade_therm.F90:151-163: the face sigma(k) flux uses the node distance stagsigma(k)-stagsigma(k-1) with stagsigma(0)=sigma(1) and stagsigma(upn)=sigma(upn)). Note the face sigma(n) is NOT midway between the nodes - the node distances and the control widths (cism_sigma_diffusion's thck*dsigma_cv) are independent geometry, both supplied by the consuming model. Positive in the +lev (downward, surface-to-bed) direction. The interface index `n` is a template PARAMETER bound to an index expression at each call site. Match-less named template. `sigma_node`, `dsigma_cv` and `thck` are the consumer's free-name geometry (this grid's contract); K is the thermal conductivity (W/m/K), the CISM constant coni = 2.1.",
   "params": ["u", "K", "n"],
   "body": {
    "op": "/",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "K",
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         { "op": "index", "args": ["u", "n"] },
         { "op": "index", "args": ["u", { "op": "-", "args": ["n", 1] }] }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "thck",
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         { "op": "index", "args": ["sigma_node", "n"] },
         { "op": "index", "args": ["sigma_node", { "op": "-", "args": ["n", 1] }] }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  "cism_sigma_diffusion": {
   "description": "Node-centered conservative finite-volume variable-coefficient vertical diffusion d/dz(K du/dz) on the CISM sigma column (state on the UPN+1 temperature nodes, index set lev_nodes): the consumer writes the compound D( {op:*, args:[K, D(u, wrt: lev_nodes)]}, wrt: lev_nodes ) and the rule fires on the whole compound at priority 10 before any plain-D rule can lower the inner derivative; it is match-scoped with where {u: {shape: [lev_nodes]}} (esm-spec 9.6.1). Interior nodes [2, UPN]: the flux-difference stencil L u[n] = ( G[n+1] - G[n] ) / ( thck * dsigma_cv[n] ), where G[n] = cism_interface_flux(u, K, n) is the CISM face flux (the node-to-node gradient) and thck*dsigma_cv[n] is the CISM control volume = the sigma LAYER [sigma(n-1), sigma(n)] (dsigma_cv[n] = sigma(n)-sigma(n-1), the layer width in sigma units, glissade_therm.F90:1471 dsigbot = 1 - stagsigma(upn-1) being the last one). Surface row (node 1): 0 - the surface temperature is a pinned Dirichlet value (temp(0) = min(0, artm), F90:843; matrix row 1 diag = 1, F90:1405-1408), so its operator row is identically zero. Bed row (node UPN+1): 0 - CISM's bed node is NOT a diffusion row: the basal matrix row is the algebraic flux-balance BC (frozen bed: temp(upn) - temp(upn-1) = (bfricflx + bhydroflx - bheatflx)*dsigbot*thck/coni, F90:1473-1476; thawed bed: temp(upn) = bpmp, F90:1497-1504), carried as algebraic laws in the consuming model. Because the boundary rows vanish, the operator telescopes only over the interior: sum over the interior of dsigma_cv[n] * L u[n] = (G[UPN+1] - G[1])/thck... the CISM closure, documented rather than enforced. A future EarthSciDiscretizations PR generalizes the boundary rows to consumer-supplied flux/Dirichlet free names and the coefficient to an interface array (the CISM case is the constant coni).",
   "params": ["u", "K"],
   "priority": 10,
   "match": {
    "op": "D",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": ["K", { "op": "D", "args": ["u"], "wrt": "lev_nodes" }]
     }
    ],
    "wrt": "lev_nodes"
   },
   "where": {
    "u": { "shape": ["lev_nodes"] }
   },
   "body": {
    "op": "makearray",
    "args": [],
    "regions": [
     [[1, 1]],
     [[2, "UPN"]],
     [[{ "op": "+", "args": ["UPN", 1] }, { "op": "+", "args": ["UPN", 1] }]]
    ],
    "values": [
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 0.0,
      "units": "W/m^3"
     },
     {
      "op": "faq",
      "output_idx": ["n"],
      "args": ["u", "K", "sigma_node", "dsigma_cv", "thck"],
      "ranges": { "n": [2, "UPN"] },
      "expr": {
       "op": "/",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "-",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "apply_expression_template",
           "args": [],
           "name": "cism_interface_flux",
           "bindings": {
            "u": "u",
            "K": "K",
            "n": { "op": "+", "args": ["n", 1] }
           }
          },
          {
           "op": "apply_expression_template",
           "args": [],
           "name": "cism_interface_flux",
           "bindings": {
            "u": "u",
            "K": "K",
            "n": "n"
           }
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "*",
         "args": [
          "thck",
          { "op": "index", "args": ["dsigma_cv", "n"] }
         ]
        }
       ]
      }
     },
     {
      "op": "const",
      "args": [],
      "value": 0.0,
      "units": "W/m^3"
     }
    ]
   }
  }
 }
}
